hadiths[16]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16376","He said: Rawh narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khusayfah, that 'Amr ibn Abdullah ibn Ka'b al-Sulami informed him, that Nafi' ibn Jubayr informed him, that 'Uthman ibn Abi al-'As came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). 'Uthman said: And in me was a pain that had almost destroyed me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hold with your right hand seven times and say: I seek refuge in the might of Allah and His power from the evil of what I find. He said: So I did that, and Allah removed what was in me, and I have not ceased commanding it to my family and others."
"16377","He said: Rawh and Abd al-Samad narrated to us, they said: Hammad narrated to us, Rawh said: al-Jurayri informed us, from Abu al-'Ala, from 'Uthman ibn Abi al-'As and a woman of Qays, that they both heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). One of them said: I heard him saying: O Allah, forgive me my sin and my mistake and my intent. And the other said: I heard him saying: O Allah, I seek Your guidance to the soundest of my affair, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of my soul."
"16378","He said: Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu al-'Ala, from 'Uthman ibn Abi al-'As, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, make me imam of my people. So he said: You are their imam, and follow the weakest of them, and take a caller who does not take a wage for his call."
"16379","'Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Sa'id al-Jurayri informed us, from Abu al-'Ala, from Mutarrif, from 'Uthman ibn Abi al-'As, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, make me imam of my people. He said: You are their imam, so follow the weakest of them, and take a caller who does not take a wage for his call."
"16380","'Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us: Sa'id al-Jurayri informed us, from Abu al-'Ala, from Mutarrif, from 'Uthman ibn Abi al-'As, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, make me imam of my people. He said: You are their imam, and follow the weakest of them, and take a caller who does not take a wage for his call."
"16381","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hind, from Mutarrif, he said: I entered upon 'Uthman ibn Abi al-'As, and he said: Indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Fasting is a shield, like the shield of one of you from fighting."
"16382","And the last of what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon me when he sent me to al-Taif was: He said: O 'Uthman, be brief in prayer, for among the people are the old and the needy."
"16383","Ishaq ibn 'Isa narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khusayfah, that 'Amr ibn Abdullah ibn Ka'b informed him, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from 'Uthman ibn Abi al-'As, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me, and in me was a pain that had almost destroyed me, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Wipe it with your right hand seven times and say: I seek refuge in the might of Allah and His power from the evil of what I find. He said: So I did that, and Allah removed what was in me, and I have not ceased commanding it to my family and others."
"16384","He said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Nu'man ibn Salim, he said: I heard our shaykhs of Thaqif, they said: 'Uthman ibn Abi al-'As informed us, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Lead your people, and when you lead your people, lighten the prayer for them, for there stand in it the young and the old and the weak and the sick and the needy."
"16385","Waki' narrated to us: 'Amr ibn 'Uthman narrated to us, from Musa ibn Talhah, from 'Uthman ibn Abi al-'As, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O 'Uthman, lead your people, and whoever leads the people, let him lighten, for among them are the weak and the old and the needy; and when you pray for yourself, pray as you wish."
"16386","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, he said: I heard Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, he said: 'Uthman ibn Abi al-'As narrated: The last of what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon me, when you lead a people, lighten the prayer for them."
"16387","He said: Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hind, that Mutarrif, of Banu 'Amir ibn Sa'sa'ah, narrated to him, that 'Uthman ibn Abi al-'As al-Thaqafi called for milk to give him to drink, so Mutarrif said: Indeed I am fasting. So 'Uthman said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Fasting is a shield from the Fire, like the shield of one of you from fighting."
"16388","And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Good fasting is the fasting of three days of the month."
"16389","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, from 'Uthman ibn Abi al-'As, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A caller calls every night: Is there a supplicant that he may be answered; is there an asker that he may be given; is there a seeker of forgiveness that he may be forgiven, until the dawn breaks."
"16390","He said: Yazid narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, he said: 'Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Hasan, he said: 'Uthman ibn Abi al-'As passed by Kilab ibn Umayyah while he was sitting in the council of the tithe at al-Basrah, and said: What makes you sit here? He said: This one has employed me upon this place, meaning Ziyad. So 'Uthman said to him: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes. So 'Uthman said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Dawud, prophet of Allah, peace be upon him, had an hour of the night in which he would wake his family and say: O household of Dawud, stand and pray, for indeed this is an hour in which Allah answers supplication, except for a sorcerer or a tithe-collector. So Kilab ibn Umayyah boarded his ship and came to Ziyad and asked to be excused, and he excused him."
"16391","'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, he said: 'Uthman ibn Abi al-'As passed by Kilab ibn Umayyah, and he mentioned similar to it."
